\section{Code snapshots}
\label{sec:metrics-snapshots}

The code metrics need files to read.
For a single window they read the working directory as it is: the
\enquote{current version} of the program.
For a series they need the program as it stood at the end of each
bucket, which is the tree of the bucket's last run---extracted with
the exporter's [[extract_code_state]] (\cref{progsnap2}), one
[[git archive]] per bucket, into a temporary directory the command
layer owns.
The trees are already free of [[.venv]] and [[__pycache__]]
([[EXCLUDE_PATTERNS]] in \cref{gitrepo}), but a repository reconstructed from
someone else's ProgSnap2 export need not be, so the file walk filters
by path component as well.

<<metrics imports>>=
import pathlib
<<metrics constants>>=
SNAPSHOT_EXCLUDED_DIRS = frozenset({
    ".venv", "venv", "env", ".learnlog", ".git", "__pycache__",
    "node_modules", "site-packages",
})
<<metrics functions>>=
def snapshot_files(root):
    """The Python files under `root`, excluding tool directories."""
    root = pathlib.Path(root)
    return sorted(
        path for path in root.rglob("*.py")
        if not set(path.relative_to(root).parts[:-1])
        & SNAPSHOT_EXCLUDED_DIRS
    )
@

A bucket label is student text---a tag name may contain [[/]] and a
merged label contains [[;]]---while the snapshot directory name is
an implementation detail nobody reads, so it is flattened to a safe
alphabet instead of escaping this class of problem one character at
a time.

<<metrics functions>>=
def snapshot_dir_name(label):
    """Flatten a bucket label into a safe directory name."""
    return re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9._-]", "_", label)
<<metrics functions>>=
def bucket_snapshot(repo, bucket, root):
    """Extract the tree of the bucket's last run under `root`.

    Returns the snapshot directory, or `None` for an empty bucket.
    """
    runs = bucket.runs
    if not runs:
        return None
    state_dir = pathlib.Path(root) / snapshot_dir_name(bucket.label)
    extract_code_state(repo, runs[-1].commit, state_dir)
    return state_dir
<<metrics test functions>>=
def test_snapshot_files_skips_tool_directories(tmp_path):
  (tmp_path / "main.py").write_text("")
  (tmp_path / "pkg").mkdir()
  (tmp_path / "pkg" / "mod.py").write_text("")
  (tmp_path / ".venv" / "lib").mkdir(parents=True)
  (tmp_path / ".venv" / "lib" / "x.py").write_text("")
  (tmp_path / "__pycache__").mkdir()
  (tmp_path / "__pycache__" / "y.py").write_text("")
  names = [p.relative_to(tmp_path).as_posix()
           for p in snapshot_files(tmp_path)]
  assert names == ["main.py", "pkg/mod.py"]
